            <div xml:id="d441">

                <pb facs="0429" n="313" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg313"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.6112/3.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-07-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 20, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>President Gómez spoke in his note (fourth paragraph) of the frequent transmission
                    through this Legation of “contradictory advice” (consejos contradictorios) in
                    this matter. It is superfluous perhaps to state that absolutely no
                    representations or observations have been made by this Legation except in the
                    note addressed to the President in obedience to the Department’s instruction
                    dated July 17.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaupré</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
